WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.868
--Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.033
You're here. You made it.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:08.100
Thank you for watching
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.834
Well, guys,
here's some good news.

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:13.200
Today, Moderna announced a new
version of their COVID booster

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.000
that's eight times stronger

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.467
and provides
longer-lasting protection.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.534
[ Cheers ]

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.000
Which sounds
less like a vaccine,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.868
more like an ad
for Right Guard deodorant.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.801
But still...

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:27.067
Seven times the protection.
yeah.

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.367
Moderna's going to have
a new shot by this fall.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.567
You know the pandemic's
been going on too long

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.167
when even the vaccines
have variants.

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:35.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.634
And people
are talking about this.

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:38.701
I saw that Elon Musk
is threatening to walk away

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:42.033
from his $44-billion deal
to buy Twitter.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:44.767
Yeah, I feel like Elon
is pretty close to saying,

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.801
"I'm so sorry.
My 2-year-old took my iPad

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.000
and clicked 'buy,'
so I didn't know what...

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
So we're cool?
We're cool, right?"

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.501
Yeah, Musk said that he reserves

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:56.868
all rights not to "consummate"
the transaction.

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:01.968
Which sounds like something Mike
Pence said on his honeymoon.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.367
-Hey, oh, whoa!

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.968
-Whoa. Hey.
Why would you do that?

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.667
-Pence!
-In other --

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.234
In other news, I read that
the Biden administration

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.234
has been trying
to contact North Korea

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:19.133
for the past month
but hasn't gotten a response.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:21.567
To be fair -- To be fair,
there's a time difference.

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.534
Here, it's about 11:40 p.m.

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.601
While in North Korea, it's 1955.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:30.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.634
"Did you get that fax yet?"
Yeah.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.734
Switching gears,
I saw that Amazon has opened

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.834
its first physical
clothing store.

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.868
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:41.901
With brands like Calvin Klein,
Lacoste, and Levi's.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.267
It's not the only exciting thing
that Amazon's working on.

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:46.734
Check out this commercial
that they just released.

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.534
-Are you tired
of how convenient it is

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.801
to go online
for all your shopping needs?

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:53.501
Wish you could go someplace
with even less stuff?

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:57.100
Introducing Amazon's
latest innovation, the Mall.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.801
It's just like
shopping on our website,

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.601
but now you get
to drive 45 minutes

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:03.067
to a drafty building
full of bored security guards

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:06.133
and cool teenagers that laugh
at you when you walk inside.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:09.234
At the Amazon Mall,
you can buy almost anything,

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:11.634
as long as it's from
these 12 stores,

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:14.767
including Auntie Anne's pretzels
and a smaller Target.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.667
And the best part --
everything here is somehow

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.400
even more expensive.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.167
Amazon's Mall, from Amazon,
The Penis Rocket People.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:27.567
-There you go.
Is that what they're call--

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:30.234
-That's their tagline now?

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:31.501
Penis Rocket!

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:34.667
-Yeah, I know, yeah.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.634
Well, some entertainment news.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:39.734
The director of "The Joker"
movie starring Joaquin Phoenix

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.334
has confirmed that
there's going to be a sequel.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:43.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.901
And the title is French.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:47.834
The title is
"Joker: Folie a Deux."

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.767
"Folie a Deux."

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:51.467
Yeah, you know moviegoers
are gonna be like,

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:54.868
"Yeah, give me two tickets
for fillet of ducks. Thanks.

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:57.234
'Joker.' The 'Joker' movie."

00:02:57.234 --> 00:03:00.167
I heard that the federal
government is investigating

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.434
complaints
from Honda Pilot owners

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:05.167
that say their engines
won't restart.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.234
Of course,
Honda immediately rebranded it

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:09.934
as the most
fuel-efficient car ever.

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:11.501
You won't...

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.267
Meanwhile, Kia owners are like,

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:16.200
"Hey, at least your car
started once. Hey. Come on."

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.667
Well, this is wild.

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:20.167
One of the largest European
drug busts ever just happened.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:23.167
Police in Italy just seized
over four tons of cocaine...

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:24.567
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.200
...with more than $250 million
worth of cocaine.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.367
250. Yeah.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.734
And we've actually zeroed in

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:31.968
on which Italian kingpin
was buying it.

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:33.501
And we actually
got footage of him.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.901
-Are you serious?
-Yeah. Watch this.

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:40.300
♪♪

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:44.701
♪♪

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:46.868
-I'm-a gonna live forever!

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:48.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:54.067
-Wow!

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.467
-He's jumping over the building.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.334
-He's jumping over everything.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:59.200
-My gosh.
-Well, get this.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.334
A man in the U.K.
set a new world record

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:06.033
after he drank at 56 pubs
in 24 hours.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.901
Yep, Guinness calls it
a world record

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:10.701
while his wife calls it
a "problem."

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.467
I'm not sure if it counts
'cause he pretty much

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.167
"Weekend at Bernie'd"
the last ten pubs.

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.667
He's like...
"Give him another one!"

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:20.300
Listen to this.
A Scottish couple

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.901
unofficially broke
a world record after they ran

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:26.501
106 marathons in 106 days...

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:28.801
answering the question,
what is the opposite of drinking

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.434
at 56 pubs in 24 hours?

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:33.167
That's what I'm talking about.
Yeah.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:36.200
[ Applause ]

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.133
"Just give him another one."

